      "page_title": "Structure First, Then Measure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "31. Derive, Don't Duplicate",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const full = first + ' ' + last;  // derive",
            "// not useState + useEffect sync",
            "// that costs an extra render pass"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Never useEffect + setState to mirror props.",
            "Use the key-reset trick or compute during render.",
            "useReducer: one dispatch, one render, many fields.",
            "React 18 batches anyway — clarity is the real win."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "32. Structural Escapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Problem",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "per-keystroke renders",
              "uncontrolled input + ref"
            ],
            [
              "10,000 rows",
              "virtualize, render 20"
            ],
            [
              "heavy list while typing",
              "useDeferredValue"
            ],
            [
              "slow non-urgent update",
              "startTransition"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "react-window / TanStack Virtual beat memoizing rows.",
            "Refs give values on submit with zero renders."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "33. DevTools Profiler"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Record an interaction, read the flamegraph: width = time.",
            "Enable 'Record why each component rendered'.",
            "Reasons: props / state / hooks / parent / context.",
            "'Highlight updates' shows the cascade live on screen."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "34. Programmatic Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "<Profiler id='list' onRender={log}>",
            "// (id, phase, actualDuration,",
            "//  baseDuration, startTime, commitTime)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "baseDuration = the cost with no memoization at all.",
            "The gap to actualDuration is what memo buys you.",
            "Always profile a production build — dev is much slower.",
            "Throttle CPU 4x or 6x to model a real device."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "35. Three Different Costs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Fix"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "too many renders",
              "memo / colocate"
            ],
            [
              "one slow render",
              "useMemo / split"
            ],
            [
              "slow commit",
              "fewer DOM mutations"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Scale, not vibes",
          "text": "60 renders at 0.1ms is fine; 2 renders at 200ms is the bug. Memoize the measured bottleneck — every memo is code you keep correct forever."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs & First Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "36. The Tool Table",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Memoizes",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "memo",
              "a component",
              "prop compare + tree"
            ],
            [
              "useMemo",
              "a value",
              "closure + deps + memory"
            ],
            [
              "useCallback",
              "a fn reference",
              "same as useMemo"
            ],
            [
              "key",
              "nothing",
              "can force a remount"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "Behaviour"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "useRef",
              "mutable, NEVER re-renders"
            ],
            [
              "useSyncExternalStore",
              "selector: only affected render"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "37. Which To Reach For"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symptom",
            "Reach for"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "child renders too much",
              "memo + stable props"
            ],
            [
              "a computation is slow",
              "useMemo"
            ],
            [
              "fn feeds a memo/effect",
              "useCallback"
            ],
            [
              "a list reorders wrong",
              "keys"
            ],
            [
              "value shouldn't render",
              "useRef"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "38. What It Costs"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Memory retained for the component's whole life.",
            "Dep arrays that quietly go stale.",
            "Harder-to-read code and comparison work every render.",
            "All-or-nothing: every prop crossing must be stable."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "fix structure",
              "then memoize",
              "then virtualize"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Compiler changes the math",
          "text": "React Compiler memoizes automatically and correctly, so hand-written memo is drifting toward a legacy, edge-case tool."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "39. Mistakes: memo"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "memo'd child + inline arrow/object/array: pure overhead.",
            "Provider value built inline: every consumer re-renders."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "40. Mistakes: Keys & Deps"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Index key on a reorderable or filterable list.",
            "State and DOM then attach to the wrong items.",
            "Random keys: remount, lost focus, scroll, animation.",
            "Omitting a dep to 'stop the loop' gives stale closures."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Gotchas & The Decision Flow",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "41. More Gotchas",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "arr.push(x); setArr(arr);  // same ref: dead",
            "setArr([...arr, x]);       // new ref: renders"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "memo does no deep compare: {a:1} vs {a:1} fails.",
            "useMemo(() => a+b, [a,b]) costs more than the add.",
            "Chasing 'zero re-renders' is not a goal; slow ones are."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "jsx",
          "lines": [
            "function Page() {",
            "  function Row(){ return <li/> }  // new type!",
            "  return <Row/>  // remounts every render",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A nested component is a new type, so state is destroyed.",
            "{...props} into a memo'd child: one hidden field kills it.",
            "Deep-equal comparators become the bottleneck themselves."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "42. Summary: Defaults"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Render = call the function; commit = touch the DOM.",
            "Most re-renders never touch the DOM at all.",
            "Re-render on: own state, parent render, context value."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "43. Identity Recap"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reconciliation matches by (type, position), then key.",
            "Different type or different key = unmount + remount.",
            "Keys are identity, not a perf knob: stable data IDs."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "44. Memo Recap"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "memo stops the parent cascade.",
            "useMemo/useCallback keep the crossing props stable.",
            "One unstable reference invalidates the whole chain."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "45. The Decision Flow"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "Is it actually slow?",
              "Move state down",
              "Pass children",
              "memo + stable props",
              "Virtualize"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Compiler era",
          "text": "React Compiler automates most of this. Write clean, pure, idiomatic components and let it memoize."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trivial Memoization",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "45. The Trivial Case",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const sum = useMemo(",
            "  () => a + b, [a, b])",
            "// hook overhead > addition cost"
          ],
          "note": "overhead exceeds work"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The hook costs more than the addition.",
            "Closure creation is not free.",
            "Dependency comparison adds CPU cycles.",
            "Memory is retained for the instance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "46. Why It Fails"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Cost",
            "Source"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "closure",
              "function allocation"
            ],
            [
              "deps",
              "Object.is checks"
            ],
            [
              "memory",
              "cache entry"
            ],
            [
              "logic",
              "branching overhead"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Simple math is nanoseconds.",
            "Hook setup is microseconds.",
            "Net result is negative performance.",
            "Code complexity increases for no gain."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "47. When To Skip"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "String concatenation of short values.",
            "Simple arithmetic operations.",
            "Boolean logic or ternaries.",
            "Array filtering with small inputs."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "items": [
            "If it fits in one line, skip it.",
            "If it is pure, just compute it.",
            "Let the compiler handle optimization.",
            "Keep render logic simple and direct."
          ],
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "48. Correct Approach"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const sum = a + b;",
            "// direct computation",
            "// no hook, no deps, no cost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Compute during render phase.",
            "No state, no side effects.",
            "React handles the diffing.",
            "Cleaner code, faster execution."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Common mistake",
          "text": "Wrapping trivial expressions in useMemo is a sign of misunderstanding the tool. It is for expensive calculations or stable references, not for simple math."
        }
      ]
    }
